  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Emergency Protection Response for internally displaced people (IDPs) in Upper Nile, Unity and Northern Jonglei states</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $2.6 million UNHCR project is to provide emergency protection services to people displaced by conflict and unprecedented floods. To that end, UNHCR will provide multi-purpose cash to 14,900 people, in-kind assistance, including core relief items and shelter support, to 13,825 people as well as comprehensive protection case management support, including referrals, targeting 23,040 people. UNHCR will also conduct awareness raising and community coherence events targeting more than 25,000 people to strengthen the overall protection environment. In total, UNHCR will reach 67,800 people, including 21,018 women, 18,984 girls and 2,610 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
